  "title": "India's E100 Flex-Fuel Vehicle Policy Update",
  "summary": "The Indian government has amended its motor vehicle rules to allow vehicles that can run on 100% ethanol fuel, with new guidelines for fuel specifications and classification thresholds. This change aims to expand access to renewable fuels for vehicles, while also raising vehicle weight limits and clarifying fuel usage.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Central Motor Vehicle Rules were amended to allow E100 fuel for vehicles.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vehicles can run on up to E100 (nearly pure ethanol) but cannot use E20 or E85.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The government raised the vehicle weight limit to 3,500 kg from 3,000 kg.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
